hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15524","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Amr ibn Kathir al-Makki informed us, he said: I asked Abd al-Rahman ibn Kaysan, mawla of Khalid ibn Usayd, I said: Will you not narrate to me from your father? And he said: What you asked me, and he said: My father narrated to me that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) come out from the kitchens until he came to the well, while he was wrapped in an izar with no rida upon him, and he saw slaves praying at the well, so he loosened the izar and wrapped himself with it and prayed two rakahs, I do not know whether Zuhr or Asr."
"15525","Hammad ibn Khalid al-Khayyat narrated to us: Amr ibn Kathir ibn Aflah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Kaysan, he said: I asked my father Kaysan: What did you witness of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I saw him praying at the upper well, the well of Banu Muti, wrapped in a garment, Zuhr or Asr, and he prayed it two rakahs."
